note Converted from the Lapis prototype, attic/lapis/app.lp.
note
note Lapis was the first attempt at this language: a PowerShell script that
note turned programs like this one into HTML. The program itself needed only
note two changes to become Shark:
note   page names are words, so `page 1` and `page 2` became One and Two
note   the welcome text says Shark rather than Lapis
note Lapis kept three byte-for-byte copies of this file (app.lp, app.lps and
note test app v1/telaviv-hub/app.lp). They are now this one file.
note
note Every button line is an original Lapis line, and Shark reads each one the
note way Lapis meant it. `Go to Final Page to page Two` keeps its whole label,
note because a bare `to` is not the ending phrase `to page`. See spec/02 2.4.2.

share Dashboard

page Dashboard
  show text Welcome to Shark!
  show button Get Started to page One

page One
  show text You have reached Page 1!
  show button Go to Final Page to page Two
  show button Back to Dashboard to page Dashboard

page Two
  show text You have reached Page 2!
  show button Return to Dashboard to page Dashboard
